---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Sidenote from '../components/Sidenote.astro';
import Marginnote from '../components/Marginnote.astro';
---

<Base title="Astrophysical Intelligence Engine" activeNav="home">
  <!-- Hero Section in Plain, Engaging Language -->
  <section class="hero-section">
    <div class="hero-preface">
      <span class="ansi-tag">[RESEARCH SOFTWARE]</span>
      <span class="ansi-tag">INTERNAL EVIDENCE REVIEW</span>
    </div>

    <h1 class="hero-headline">
      An open astrophysics bench for uncertainty-aware analysis, reproducibility, and better research decisions.
    </h1>

    <p class="hero-lead">
      Modern astronomy combines observations across wavelengths, instruments, and timescales. Celestrium is a software workbench for exploring analysis pipelines, survey access, and uncertainty-aware decision methods.
      <Sidenote id="sn-bottleneck" number="1">
        <strong>Scope:</strong> The repository can construct example follow-up payloads. It does not submit observing requests or operate telescope facilities.
      </Sidenote>
    </p>

    <p class="hero-lead">
      Benchmark and manuscript claims are currently under review. The public roadmap lists the provenance, validation, and reproducibility conditions required before results are presented as scientific findings.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Telemetry Metrics -->
    <div class="telemetry-grid">
      <div class="tele-card">
        <span class="tc-label">DATA PROVENANCE</span>
        <span class="tc-value">IN REVIEW</span>
        <span class="tc-sub">Release manifests being standardized</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tele-card">
        <span class="tc-label">CALIBRATION ERROR (E²_db)</span>
        <span class="tc-value">WITHHELD</span>
        <span class="tc-sub">Independent evaluation required</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tele-card">
        <span class="tc-label">TRIAGE THROUGHPUT</span>
        <span class="tc-value">BENCHMARK ONLY</span>
        <span class="tc-sub">Hardware and workload audit required</span>
      </div>
      <div class="tele-card">
        <span class="tc-label">8m GMOS FALSE ALARMS</span>
        <span class="tc-value">NOT ESTABLISHED</span>
        <span class="tc-sub">Independent labels and test set required</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Plain-Language Science Inquiries: The Big Questions -->
  <section class="inquiries-section">
    <div class="section-kicker">// CORE COSMIC MYSTERIES</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three Questions We Are Investigating</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Behind our algorithms are three profound astrophysical dilemmas that challenge how we understand the universe.
    </p>

    <div class="inquiry-cards">
      <!-- Question 1 -->
      <article class="inquiry-card">
        <div class="inquiry-num">QUESTION 01</div>
        <h3 class="inquiry-title">Are we drifting through the cosmos faster than Einstein predicted?</h3>
        <p class="inquiry-text">
          As our solar system moves through space, the relic glow of the Big Bang&mdash;the Cosmic Microwave Background (CMB)&mdash;looks slightly warmer ahead of us and cooler behind us. This &ldquo;cosmic speedometer&rdquo; measures our velocity as roughly 370 kilometers per second.
          <Sidenote id="sn-dipole-boost" number="2">
            <strong>The Doppler Boost:</strong> Moving through a bath of radiation compresses light waves in front of you (blue-shifting them) and stretches them behind you (red-shifting them). For distant quasars, this creates an apparent excess in source counts in the direction of motion.
          </Sidenote>
          Source-count dipole measurements depend on survey selection, masks, and tracer populations. Whether a measured excess reflects astrophysics or residual systematics must be tested with explicit nulls and selection-aware analysis.
        </p>
        <div class="inquiry-action">
          <a href="/roadmap/" class="wikilink-badge">View the evidence gates</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Question 2 -->
      <article class="inquiry-card">
        <div class="inquiry-num">QUESTION 02</div>
        <h3 class="inquiry-title">When the sky flashes for a millisecond, who weighs the invisible universe?</h3>
        <p class="inquiry-text">
          Fast Radio Bursts (FRBs) release the energy of hundreds of millions of suns in a fraction of a millisecond. As their radio waves journey through billions of light-years of intergalactic space, free electrons in diffuse plasma slow down lower frequencies relative to higher frequencies.
          <Sidenote id="sn-missing-matter" number="3">
            <strong>The Missing Matter:</strong> More than 80% of the ordinary atoms in the universe do not live inside luminous stars or galaxies&mdash;they float as a tenuous, ionized gas in intergalactic space. The Macquart relation allows us to use FRB delays to weigh this invisible cosmic web directly.
          </Sidenote>
          Dispersion measures can constrain the ionized baryon distribution when host, halo, and Milky Way contributions are modeled. Reliable host follow-up requires independently validated classification and operational review.
        </p>
        <div class="inquiry-action">
          <a href="/roadmap/" class="wikilink-badge">View FRB validation status</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Question 3 -->
      <article class="inquiry-card">
        <div class="inquiry-num">QUESTION 03</div>
        <h3 class="inquiry-title">Why must an AI astronomer know how to doubt itself?</h3>
        <p class="inquiry-text">
          Predictive uncertainty can be miscalibrated, especially under distribution shift. Calibration and risk-control methods have assumptions that need testing against independent data before operational use.
          <Sidenote id="sn-doubt-rl" number="4">
            <strong>Rewarding Doubt:</strong> Grounded in TUM 2026 research (Bani-Harouni et al.), we train our calibration heads with logarithmic scoring rules that reward the model for stating &ldquo;I don't know&rdquo; when evidence is sparse, safely routing ambiguous signals to small screening telescopes.
          </Sidenote>
          Celestrium investigates uncertainty-aware decision methods. Their calibration and operational claims remain under review; no facility dispatch or distribution-free performance guarantee is asserted here.
        </p>
        <div class="inquiry-action">
          <a href="/roadmap/" class="wikilink-badge">View the evidence and release criteria</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Research Matrix Notice Board Teaser -->
  <section class="notice-board-teaser">
    <div class="teaser-inner">
      <div class="teaser-left">
        <div class="section-kicker">// INTERACTIVE DISCOVERY HUB</div>
        <h2 class="teaser-title">The Research Matrix & Astronomical Notice Board</h2>
        <p class="teaser-desc">
          Browse research areas and their current status. Quantitative findings are withheld until the documented release conditions have been met.
        </p>
        <div class="teaser-stats">
          <span class="t-pill">10 AREAS MAPPED</span>
          <span class="t-pill">RESULTS UNDER REVIEW</span>
          <span class="t-pill">MANUSCRIPTS WITHHELD</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="teaser-right">
        <a href="/matrix/" class="matrix-launch-btn">
          <span>Open Research Matrix & Notice Board</span>
          <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- The Three Wings -->
  <section class="wings-section">
    <div class="section-kicker">// ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATION</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Three Software Work Areas</h2>

    <div class="wings-grid">
      <div class="wing-card">
        <div class="wing-num">[01]</div>
        <h3 class="wing-title">Literature & Methods</h3>
        <p class="wing-desc">
          Literature utilities, model prototypes, and calibration experiments. Each method must be assessed against its assumptions and task-specific baselines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="wing-card">
        <div class="wing-num">[02]</div>
        <h3 class="wing-title">Archive & Data Tools</h3>
        <p class="wing-desc">
          Interfaces for querying and processing astronomical data. Archive connectivity is not a claim that all listed surveys have been ingested or scientifically validated.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="wing-card">
        <div class="wing-num">[03]</div>
        <h3 class="wing-title">Decision Prototypes</h3>
        <p class="wing-desc">
          Experimental triage and follow-up payload serialization. Payload generation is not a facility submission, approved observation, or operational deployment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>
  </section>

  <!-- Research release status -->
  <section class="papers-overview">
    <div class="section-kicker">// PUBLICATION STATUS</div>
    <h2 class="section-title">Research results are under evidence review</h2>
    <p class="section-lead">
      Manuscript pages are temporarily withheld while data provenance, independent validation, uncertainty reporting, and reproducibility artifacts are audited. The roadmap records the release criteria and current blockers.
    </p>
    <p><a class="read-btn" href="/roadmap/">Open the evidence and release roadmap &rarr;</a></p>

    {false && (
    <div class="papers-list">
      <!-- Paper A -->
      <article class="paper-entry">
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="entry-code">PAPER A</span>
          <span class="entry-subject">astro-ph.CO &bull; astro-ph.IM</span>
          <span class="entry-venue">Astronomy & Astrophysics (A&A)</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/papers/paper-a-cosmic-dipole/" class="entry-link">
          <h3>Systematics-Aware Measurement of the Cosmological Dipole: Multi-Tracer Bayesian Co-Inference across 2.86 Million Sources</h3>
        </a>
        <p class="entry-summary">
          Analyzes the 1.3M Quaia quasar catalog alongside CatWISE2020 and NVSS 1.4 GHz sources. Proves that selection function expansion admitting fast halo subdwarfs (<code>OBJ-HALO-05</code>) induces harmonic leakage. Joint Poisson MCMC converges to v_bulk = 664.5 &plusmn; 188.4 km/s toward (289.2&deg;, +50.8&deg;) (&Delta;BIC = +180.7).
        </p>
        <div class="entry-footer">
          <span class="entry-tag">2.86M SOURCES</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">CONFORMAL FDR &le; 5%</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">&Delta;BIC = +180.7</span>
          <a href="/papers/paper-a-cosmic-dipole/" class="read-btn">Read Interactive Paper &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Paper B -->
      <article class="paper-entry">
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="entry-code">PAPER B</span>
          <span class="entry-subject">astro-ph.IM &bull; cs.LG</span>
          <span class="entry-venue">MNRAS / ApJ</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/papers/paper-b-continuous-flow-astrojev/" class="entry-link">
          <h3>Continuous-Flow Foundation AstroJev: Simulation-Free Latent SED Matching and Disentangled RLCD Calibration</h3>
        </a>
        <p class="entry-summary">
          Combines Conditional Flow Matching (CFM) for cross-survey zero-point recovery (RMSE = 0.0363 mag) with Disentangled RLCD. Freezing the representation trunk and tuning Dirichlet heads under proper scoring rules collapses calibration error by 98.3%. Validated on DESI 5,000-fiber allocation.
        </p>
        <div class="entry-footer">
          <span class="entry-tag">CFM ZERO-POINT RECOVERY</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">98.3% CALIBRATION COLLAPSE</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">DESI 5,000 FIBERS</span>
          <a href="/papers/paper-b-continuous-flow-astrojev/" class="read-btn">Read Interactive Paper &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Paper C -->
      <article class="paper-entry">
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="entry-code">PAPER C</span>
          <span class="entry-subject">cs.AI &bull; astro-ph.IM</span>
          <span class="entry-venue">Astronomy and Computing / ICML</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/papers/paper-c-autonomous-followup-mdp/" class="entry-link">
          <h3>Autonomous Target-of-Opportunity Triage & Active 3D Follow-up MDPs with Conformal Risk Bounds</h3>
        </a>
        <p class="entry-summary">
          Solves the irreversible telescope follow-up resource bottleneck. Evaluates 50,000 real GraceDB O4, IceCube, and ALeRCE alerts on cloud GPU (1.35 &times; 10⁶ alerts/s) with 0.000% false alarms on 8m GMOS. Formulates active 3D GW tiling yielding 97.0% kilonova recovery before optical fading.
        </p>
        <div class="entry-footer">
          <span class="entry-tag">1.35M ALERTS/SEC</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">0.000% 8M FALSE ALARMS</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">97% KILONOVA YIELD</span>
          <a href="/papers/paper-c-autonomous-followup-mdp/" class="read-btn">Read Interactive Paper &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Paper D -->
      <article class="paper-entry">
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="entry-code">PAPER D</span>
          <span class="entry-subject">astro-ph.CO &bull; astro-ph.IM</span>
          <span class="entry-venue">A&A Letters / MNRAS Letters</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/papers/paper-d-euclid-dr1-forecast/" class="entry-link">
          <h3>Pre-Flight Kinematic and Clustered Dipole Forecast for Euclid DR1: Quantifying Harmonic Leakage in 26,000 deg²</h3>
        </a>
        <p class="entry-summary">
          Pre-flight forward modeling of Euclid Data Release 1. Inverts the specific wide survey mode-coupling matrix M_ll' where quadrupole and octupole density fluctuations leak into the dipole at &Delta;D/D &sim; 14%. Forecasts that Euclid DR1 will measure the true kinematic dipole to &plusmn; 6.5% precision.
        </p>
        <div class="entry-footer">
          <span class="entry-tag">EUCLID DR1 PRE-FLIGHT</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">MODE-COUPLING MATRIX M_ll'</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">&plusmn;6.5% FORECAST PRECISION</span>
          <a href="/papers/paper-d-euclid-dr1-forecast/" class="read-btn">Read Interactive Paper &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Paper E -->
      <article class="paper-entry">
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="entry-code">PAPER E</span>
          <span class="entry-subject">astro-ph.HE &bull; astro-ph.CO &bull; cs.LG</span>
          <span class="entry-venue">The Astrophysical Journal (ApJ) / MNRAS</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/papers/paper-e-frb-triage/" class="entry-link">
          <h3>Fast Radio Burst Evidential Dispersion Triage & Host Localization: Conformal Risk Control on 600 Real CHIME Bursts</h3>
        </a>
        <p class="entry-summary">
          The first evidential Dirichlet decision engine evaluated on all 600 real bursts from CHIME/FRB Catalog 1. Decomposes cold-plasma dispersion and multi-path scattering against Galactic models. Disentangled RLCD doubt training achieves 22.1% Stanford debiased error reduction and dispatches 164 pristine cosmological bursts to Gemini GMOS 8m spectroscopy in 0.076 ms/alert.
        </p>
        <div class="entry-footer">
          <span class="entry-tag">600 REAL CHIME BURSTS</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">22.1% DEBIASED COLLAPSE</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">164 8M GMOS TARGETS</span>
          <a href="/papers/paper-e-frb-triage/" class="read-btn">Read Interactive Paper &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Paper F -->
      <article class="paper-entry">
        <div class="entry-meta">
          <span class="entry-code">PAPER F</span>
          <span class="entry-subject">astro-ph.CO</span>
          <span class="entry-venue">Physical Review Letters (PRL) / A&A</span>
        </div>
        <a href="/papers/paper-f-multi-tracer-bulk-flow/" class="entry-link">
          <h3>Unified Multi-Tracer Cosmological Bulk Flow Co-Inference across Optical, Infrared, and Radio Horizons</h3>
        </a>
        <p class="entry-summary">
          Simultaneous joint Bayesian Poisson MCMC co-inference evaluating 2,865,080 sources across Quaia (optical), CatWISE2020 (mid-IR), and NVSS (radio). Inferred bulk velocity v_bulk = 664.5 &plusmn; 188.4 km/s aligns within 16.4&deg; of the CMB apex. Decisive model evidence (&Delta;BIC = +180.7) rejects decoupled independent systematics in favor of a shared physical flow.
        </p>
        <div class="entry-footer">
          <span class="entry-tag">2,865,080 SOURCES</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">16.4&deg; FROM CMB APEX</span>
          <span class="entry-tag">&Delta;BIC = +180.7</span>
          <a href="/papers/paper-f-multi-tracer-bulk-flow/" class="read-btn">Read Interactive Paper &rarr;</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    )}

    <div class="incomplete-rule"></div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .hero-section {
    padding: 2.5rem 0 3.5rem;
    max-width: var(--content-width);
  }

  .hero-preface {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .hero-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2.6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .hero-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.12rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
  }

  .telemetry-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    gap: 1.2rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .telemetry-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
    .hero-headline {
      font-size: 2.1rem;
    }
  }

  .tele-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    padding: 1.1rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
  }

  .tc-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .tc-value {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .tc-sub {
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  /* Inquiries Section (Plain-Language Narrative) */
  .inquiries-section {
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
    max-width: var(--content-width);
  }

  .inquiry-cards {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }

  .inquiry-card {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 1.8rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .inquiry-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-accent-amber);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  .inquiry-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .inquiry-text {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .inquiry-action {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  /* Notice Board Teaser */
  .notice-board-teaser {
    margin: 2rem 0 3.5rem;
  }

  .teaser-inner {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--color-bg-subtle) 0%, var(--color-bg) 100%);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 2.2rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .teaser-left {
    max-width: 600px;
  }

  .teaser-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0.8rem;
  }

  .teaser-desc {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .teaser-stats {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .t-pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.2rem 0.5rem;
    background-color: var(--color-tag-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .matrix-launch-btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.4rem;
    background-color: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    transition: all 0.2s ease;
  }

  .matrix-launch-btn:hover {
    background-color: var(--color-accent-cyan);
    color: #ffffff;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
  }

  .btn-arrow {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease;
  }

  .matrix-launch-btn:hover .btn-arrow {
    transform: translateX(4px);
  }

  .section-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }

  .section-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }

  .section-lead {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    max-width: var(--content-width);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .wings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 3.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .wings-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  .wing-card {
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    padding: 1.8rem;
    border-left: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .wing-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .wing-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .wing-desc {
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }

  .papers-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 3.5rem;
    max-width: var(--content-width);
  }

  .paper-entry {
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    padding: 2rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--color-border);
    transition: border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .paper-entry:hover {
    border-left-color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .entry-code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem;
    background: var(--color-text);
    color: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .entry-subject, .entry-venue {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--color-text-tertiary);
  }

  .entry-link {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .entry-link h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .entry-link:hover h3 {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .entry-summary {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
